  "$comment": "D&D 5e (SRD) classes and the heroes who play them. Every hero is a human: the +1 to all six abilities is already in their scores. Their scores are the starting point of the point buy the player does in the first safe room (27 points, 8 to 15, src/rules/PointBuy.ts); the standard array (15, 14, 13, 12, 10, 8) placed as the class's quick build suggests costs exactly 27, so it is also what a player who changes nothing keeps. classes: hitDie (hit points = hit die + CON modifier at level 1, then the die's average + CON a level, as in the SRD, see src/rules/HitPoints.ts); armor: light, medium, heavy, shield; weapons: simple, martial; weaponBases: single weapons trained beyond those (names from src/rules/WeaponTable.ts); savingThrows: the two trained saves (they add the proficiency bonus, spell saves included); spellcasting: the ability spells use (null: not a caster); progression: per level 1-20, a list of rewards: {feature: id} (CLASS_FEATURES in src/rules/Classes.ts), {spell: id} (src/data/spells.json; spells show in the quick bar in the order learnt), {asi: true} (an Ability Score Improvement: the player puts +2 in one ability or +1 in two, no score above 20, or takes a feat from src/data/feats.json instead), {choice: fighting_style} (the player picks one, src/rules/FightingStyles.ts; a second one is a Champion's at the level it comes) or {choice: archetype} (the Fighter's Martial Archetype, src/rules/Archetypes.ts), {ability: stat, amount: n} (a fixed bonus), {feat: id} (a feat the class itself grants). Hit points, proficiency bonus, spell DC and attack follow the level on their own. SRD features not in play yet (so not listed): Expertise, Cunning Action, Arcane Recovery, Bardic Inspiration, Channel Divinity, Pact Magic slots, Eldritch Invocations other than Agonizing Blast, subclasses beyond Life and Fiend. heroes: named after their class (a second hero of a class gets a 2: fighter2); character is the sprite set (src/characters/), class one of classes.